menu "Dispenser V2 platform"

config DSP_SNTP_SERVER
    string "SNTP server"
    default "pool.ntp.org"
    help
        NTP server used for time synchronization (UTC). One server; the
        domain decides whether a received time is accepted.

config DSP_NOTIFY_URL
    string "Notification endpoint (HTTPS)"
    default "https://dispenser-notify.nowassek.workers.dev/api/v1/events"
    help
        Protocol-v1 ingestion endpoint (cloudflare/dispenser-notify). Must start
        with https://. Not a secret; the device token lives only in the
        "nvs_sec" partition. Automated tests never use this URL.

config DSP_NOTIFY_HEALTH_URL
    string "Backend health URL (diagnostic TLS probe)"
    default "https://dispenser-notify.nowassek.workers.dev/health"
    help
        Unauthenticated GET used only by the off-by-default HTTPS diagnostic to
        verify Wi-Fi, trusted time and certificate validation without sending
        an event or a credential.

config DSP_BUTTON_WAKE_GPIO
    int "Button deep-sleep wake GPIO (-1 = none; pending hardware review)"
    range -1 21
    default -1
    help
        GPIO for the service-mode button wake (M1.9c provision only). -1 keeps
        the button wake disabled, which is the required setting until the
        hardware review assigns a pin from the board pinout. Only ESP32-C3
        deep-sleep wake pads GPIO0-GPIO5 are accepted, and the strapping pin
        GPIO2 is rejected at run time; an invalid value leaves timer-only wake.
        Configures an input wake only, never an output.

config DSP_BUTTON_WAKE_ACTIVE_HIGH
    bool "Button wake level is high"
    default n
    help
        Wake on a high level (default: low level with a pull-up). Depends on
        the button circuit, to be decided by the hardware review.

endmenu
